</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain how Simpson's paradox can arise from combining strata.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Distinguish confounding from effect modification.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why sparse contingency tables can invalidate ordinary chi-square
approximations.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the asymptotic chi-square distribution of Pearson's <m>X^2</m>
statistic.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
